      "id": "casey-mears",
      "wikidata": "Q1047250",
      "summary": {
        "text": "Casey James Mears (born March 12, 1978) is an American professional off-road and stock car racing driver. He last competed part-time in the NASCAR Cup Series, driving the No. 66 Ford Mustang Dark Horse for Garage 66, and the No. 62 Chevrolet Camaro ZL1 for Beard Motorsports. He has raced in IndyCar, NASCAR's three national series, including fifteen seasons in the Cup Series, SCORE International, and the Stadium Super Trucks. A former winner of the Coca-Cola 600, Mears is a member of the Mears racing family as the nephew of four-time Indianapolis 500 winner Rick Mears and the son of IndyCar and off-road veteran Roger Mears.",
        "lang": "en",
        "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Casey_Mears"
